{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tbl-tm-interactions-table1-data","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Table","doco:Table"],"label":"tbl:tm-interactions-table1-data","kind":"table","title":"Table 1 from tm-interactions","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tm-interactions"],"tags":["extracted-table"],"text":"tm-interactions-table1-data.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"tbl:tm-interactions-table1-data\"></a><p>The explicit <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2 \\times 2</code> entries of the universal beta-decay interaction matrix <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta_\\beta(q) = \\tfrac{1}{2}(q - q^{-1})\\,\\mathbb{I}</code>: it is scalar, so only the two diagonal entries are nonzero.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th align=\"center\">Entry</th>\n<th>Formula</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(1,1)</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\frac{q - q^{-1}}{2}</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(1,2)</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(2,1)</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(2,2)</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\frac{q - q^{-1}}{2}</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-transfer-matrices/tm-interactions-table1-data.md","heading":"Table"}
